Inspect and compact the metadata log of the drives (servers started with
--metadata-log): the segments, the share of their bytes still live, the objects
indexed and the memory of the index, the group commits since the start.

Usage:
  nexoctl admin metadata-log [flags]
  nexoctl admin metadata-log [command]

Available Commands:
  compact     Compact the metadata log of the drives of a node now
  status      Show the metadata log of every drive of the deployment

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for metadata-log

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl admin metadata-log [command] --help" for more information about a command.
